  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Innovations and Multi-Sectoral Partnerships to Achieve Control of Tuberculosis (IMPACT)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Philippines):  Innovations and Multi-Sectoral Partnerships to Achieve Control of Tuberculosis (IMPACT) is a five-year activity that supports the National TB Control Program&apos;s Philippine Plan of Action to Control TB in 44 provinces and cities with the greatest TB burden and lowest performance in case detection and cure rates. FY 2016 funds will be used to:Improve capacity of health providers to diagnose, register, report, and treat TB cases;Expand the use of rapid diagnostic tests and remote smearing stations to intensify case finding among vulnerable groups;Mainstream the Programmatic Management of Multidrug-resistant TB;Conduct local TB communication campaigns to reinforce national messages;Strengthen information management, human resources, and M&amp;E; Link private laboratories to the national laboratory network and support development of an external quality assurance system; andStrengthen capacity for community-level leadership, management and governance of health services...</narrative>
  </description>
